    },
    {
      "id": "tradeoffs-text",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1224,
      "y": 1360,
      "width": 1076.4,
      "height": 292.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#514732",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 58,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1058,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TRADEOFFS / Opinion, not measured advantage\n\n• More body width, less peripheral context: inspecting another sender needs Back.\n  Preserve exact list/body positions; do not quietly replace the current message.\n• Collapsed metadata reduces noise but makes image blocking and full labels one step away.\n  Keep the labeled Details / images control; never bury load failures in that disclosure.\n• Review mode avoids a cramped drawer, but interrupts reading for batch inspection.\n  Back restores the body; the pending/error count remains visible when review is closed.\n• Removing Auto-apply and changing Ctrl+Enter adds friction for fast triagers.\n  This deliberately favors deliberation; disclose the behavior change, never switch silently.\n\nNative risk: WebView2 is a child window, not ordinary GPUI paint. Review must hide it,\nnot draw over it. Reuse the reader and restore scroll/focus; verify on Windows.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TRADEOFFS / Opinion, not measured advantage\n\n• More body width, less peripheral context: inspecting another sender needs Back.\n  Preserve exact list/body positions; do not quietly replace the current message.\n• Collapsed metadata reduces noise but makes image blocking and full labels one step away.\n  Keep the labeled Details / images control; never bury load failures in that disclosure.\n• Review mode avoids a cramped drawer, but interrupts reading for batch inspection.\n  Back restores the body; the pending/error count remains visible when review is closed.\n• Removing Auto-apply and changing Ctrl+Enter adds friction for fast triagers.\n  This deliberately favors deliberation; disclose the behavior change, never switch silently.\n\nNative risk: WebView2 is a child window, not ordinary GPUI paint. Review must hide it,\nnot draw over it. Reuse the reader and restore scroll/focus; verify on Windows.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
