  "acceptanceReport": "```acceptance-report\n{\n  \"criteriaSatisfied\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"criterion-1\",\n      \"status\": \"satisfied\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Returned a 62-element editable Excalidraw design with source-backed observations, four proposed changes, a focused reading wireframe, an outcome-recovery state, explicit safety semantics, tradeoffs and a checkable synthetic usability test.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"changedFiles\": [],\n  \"testsAddedOrUpdated\": [],\n  \"commandsRun\": [],\n  \"validationOutput\": [\n    \"Read the current working-tree source and required documentation; did not assume HEAD represented the baseline.\",\n    \"Manually reviewed the proposal against preview, selection, unread, staging, Apply and unknown-outcome contracts.\",\n    \"No application execution or Excalidraw import validation performed.\"\n  ],\n  \"residualRisks\": [\n    \"Excalidraw rendering and actual font metrics have not been runtime-validated.\",\n    \"Windows WebView2 visibility, focus and scroll restoration require native prototype validation.\",\n    \"Accessibility, small-window scaling and reading-efficiency benefits remain untested.\",\n    \"Removing Auto-apply and changing shortcut behavior require explicit later approval and migration communication.\"\n  ],\n  \"noStagedFiles\": false,\n  \"diffSummary\": \"Read-only design exploration; no repository changes made by this agent. Runtime will persist the returned artifact.\",\n  \"reviewFindings\": [\n    \"Design hypotheses are distinguished from observed source behavior; no implementation defect or merge recommendation is asserted.\"\n  ],\n  \"manualNotes\": \"Independently inspected current-layout.md, main.rs, reader.rs, gpui-poc/README.md and GOAL.md. No sibling reviews, credentials, Gmail access, program launches or delegated work. Git staging was not inspected; noStagedFiles is not attested.\"\n}\n```"
